# skill: queue-static

## Contract

Static queue backed by a static linked list allocator. Provides FIFO operations with no dynamic memory allocation. All nodes are pre-allocated from a fixed pool.

**Struct:**
- `StaticQueue` — wraps `StaticLinkedList`

**Functions:**
- `queue_init(q)` — initializes an empty queue
- `queue_enqueue(q, val)` — appends `val` to the rear; O(n) traversal, no heap allocation
- `queue_dequeue(q)` — removes and returns front element; returns underlying list value
- `queue_is_empty(q)` — returns true if queue has zero elements

**Behavior:**
- `queue_dequeue` on empty queue delegates to `ll_pop_front` (see linked-list-static contract)
- `queue_enqueue` allocates from the static node pool; silently fails if pool is exhausted

## Dependencies

- `linked-list-static` — must be loaded first; `StaticLinkedList`, `ll_init`, `ll_push_front`, `ll_pop_front`, `ll_alloc_node`, `LL_NULL`

## Slots

- `LL_NODEPOOL_SIZE` — inherited from `linked-list-static`; determines max queue capacity

## Boundaries

| Condition | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| `queue_dequeue` on empty | Delegates to `ll_pop_front` |
| `queue_enqueue` when pool full | Silently returns; no allocation |
| Queue at capacity | Same as pool exhaustion |

## Examples

```c
struct StaticQueue q;
queue_init(&q);
queue_enqueue(&q, 10);
queue_enqueue(&q, 20);
queue_dequeue(&q);  // returns 10
queue_is_empty(&q); // false
```

## Code

```c
struct StaticQueue {
    struct StaticLinkedList list;
};

void queue_init(struct StaticQueue* q) {
    ll_init(&q->list);
}

void queue_enqueue(struct StaticQueue* q, int val) {
    if (q->list.size == 0) {
        ll_push_front(&q->list, val);
        return;
    }
    int curr = q->list.nodes[0].next;
    while (q->list.nodes[curr].next != LL_NULL) {
        curr = q->list.nodes[curr].next;
    }
    int new_node = ll_alloc_node(&q->list);
    if (new_node == LL_NULL) return;
    q->list.nodes[new_node].data = val;
    q->list.nodes[new_node].next = LL_NULL;
    q->list.nodes[curr].next = new_node;
}

int queue_dequeue(struct StaticQueue* q) {
    return ll_pop_front(&q->list);
}

int queue_is_empty(struct StaticQueue* q) {
    return q->list.size == 0;
}
```
